590 0 obj
<<
/ActualText (KEY FEATURES\nLoad the Provided Data\nLoad the model price table, seed tenants, and gateway config \(model_pricing.json, seed_keys.json, gateway_config.sample.json\).\nPreserve seed key values and alias names - the demo flow and scripts reference them.\nUnified Chat Completions API\nOne OpenAI-compatible POST /v1/chat/completions endpoint in front of at least 2 providers \(mocks count\).\nCallers use a model alias/name; the gateway resolves it and never exposes provider credentials.\nEvery response carries the header contract: x-prism-provider, x-prism-cache, x-prism-fallback, x-prism-cost-usd.\nStreaming Pass-Through\n"stream": true flows tokens from provider \222 gateway \222 client as they arrive, no buffering.\nStream terminates correctly \(data: [DONE]\); usage/cost still recorded.\nVirtual Keys, Rate Limits & Budgets\nAuthenticate every request with a virtual key.\nEnforce per-key model allowlist, requests-per-minute limit, and monthly cost budget.\nDistinct, documented error per rejection type \(invalid key, model not allowed, rate limited, budget exhausted\).\nRouting, Retries & Failover\nResolve aliases \(fast, smart\) to a primary model with an ordered fallback chain.\nRetry transient errors with exponential backoff; fail over and record it.\(\nSmart Routing - the auto Alias\n"model": "auto" lets the gateway classify prompt difficulty and route to fast or smart.\nMust beat a length-only baseline - the eval set deliberately includes short-but-hard and long-but-trivial traps.\nOne-command routing eval reporting accuracy per case.)
/K [1]
/S /Span
/Type /StructElem
/P 591 0 R
/Pg 395 0 R
